    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d587">

                <pb facs="0651" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/8111: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-04">August 4,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received August 5—12:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>412. From Apodaga<anchor n="88" xml:id="d587-f1"/> to Bicknell,<anchor n="89"
                        xml:id="d587-f2"/> Rubber Reserve Company. As feasible way of promptly
                    concluding negotiations suggest compromise on Panama’s counterproposal. We might
                    allocate from development fund provided in article VII an average of $15,000
                    annually to reimburse bank upon presentation of proper vouchers for expenses of
                    warehousing, handling and delivery of rubber aboard ship for sale to Rubber
                    Reserve at 33 cents f.o.b. steamer. Bank to handle all shipping details. This
                    would meet their demand while literally retaining <pb facs="0652" n="638"
                        xml:id="pg638"/> our uniform price. If suggestion meets your approval I can
                    present it to bank next week. [Apodaca.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d587-f1" n="88" xml:id="d587-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably J. L. Apodaca, official of Rubber Reserve Company.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d587-f2" n="89" xml:id="d587-f2-content">
                <p>John W. Bicknell, vice president, Rubber Reserve Company.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
